  "text": "CG\nЦГ\nEN\nPress room\nAll news\nOrganization\nDocument library\nAccessibility\nHomepage\nMinistry of Foreign Affairs\nDiplomatic missions\nEmbassies and consulates of Montenegro and visa regimes for foreign citizens\nIreland\nIreland*\nEmbassies and consulates of Montenegro and visa regimes for foreign citizens\nContact\nEmbassy of Montenegro in United Kingdom\nVisa regime\nNationals of Ireland may enter, pass through the territory of and stay in Montenegro up to 90 days, with a valid travel document, without a visa.\nNationals of Ireland may enter, pass through the territory of and stay in Montenegro up to 30 days, without a visa, with a valid identity card issued by the competent authority of Ireland.\nDiplomatic relations\nIreland recognized Montenegro's independence on June 20, 2016, when diplomatic relations between the two countries were established.\nThe Embassy of Montenegro in the United Kingdom, based in London, is in charge for diplomatic representation of Montenegro in Ireland. Until appointment of the new ambassador, the Embassy of Montenegro is represented by charge d'affairs a.i.\nAmbassador of Ireland to Montenegro, based in Budapest, is Ragnar Almqvist.\nHomepage\nPress room\nAll news\nOrganization\nDocument library\nAsk the Government\nPR contacts\nFacebook\nX\nInstagram\nYouTube\nFlickr\nePayment\neHealth\neGovernment\nеTax\neEnrollment\nCentral Register of Business Entities\nAccessibility\nSite map\nEnglish\n©Copyright 2026. Government of MontenegroOpšti uslovi korišćenjaThis site is protected by reCAPTCHA and applies Googleprivacy policyandterms of serice.",
